      en: "The former capital of the Kingdom of Nobatia, known for Christian frescoes saved before the flooding. Flooded by Lake Nasser. Frescoes in museums. Former bishopric. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of Sudan along the Nile, the Nubian Desert and the Red Sea, and offers insight into the ancient Nubian heritage and the regional identity. Located in the Northeast African state of Sudan. The region is shaped by the Nile and the Nubian Desert. Climate is mostly hot and dry, with desert and Sahel zones."
